{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Resumed. origin/main replicated and advanced to 9808b1217; worktree reset to it (both my merged commits 23e51a014 and 87478f047 confirmed ancestors). Bug 1f32 IS fixed: merged as 095c4afef, grandfathering live per ADR 0053 (attest.py:675, attest_gate.py:169), ADR Accepted, tests landed. It was only stranded in_progress because session 2c25665e ended before closing it. Operator approved closing it on their behalf. First close attempt FAILED completion verification - correctly: the AC needs one test that rotates the registry AND drifts a dep file on a SCOPED attestation asserting stale-code, and it was absent FROM MY STALE WORKTREE. Verified independently that it does exist on main (3e2747816, change 967 MERGED, test_regver_drift_does_not_mask_code_drift_on_a_scoped_attestation); my worktree was simply behind. After updating, close passed. Closed with --class plan_defect (my classification, documented on the ticket: ADR 0053 says ADR 0015's mechanism stands and only the CONSEQUENCE changes, so the original remedy was too blunt by design - not a regression). UNBLOCKED 2aa6. Continuing the epic: 2aa6 -> {93d0, 44c7} -> 5f4d."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785009933863936001,"uuid":"6da6d77e-551f-440a-b9b4-2b54ee320b11"}